This MATLAB software implements a mixture of Gaussians variational approximation with global and local boostings for estimating
the random effects logistic regression model with bimodal priors.

How to run the copula of the mixture variational approximation

I have provided you with the .mat file containing the variational parameters for the first component of the mixture under Result folder.

The main matlab code is the gmmCopSkew_general.m

initialisation_mix2_general.m

-- to obtain the initial values for mu.

gmmCopSkew_general.m

-- main file used to obtain the variational parameters of the mixture with natural gradients.

gmmCop_mubdweight.m

-- Main file used to obtain the variational parameters of the mixture without natural gradients.

inverse_fisher_times_grad.m

-- obtaining the inverse of fisher information matrix multiply with gradient of the lower bound for updating B and d.

inverse_fisher_times_grad_onlyD.m

-- obtaining the inverse of fisher information matrix multiply with gradient of the lower bound for updating d only.

LogisticLogPosteriorSkewmix.m

-- calculate log posterior.

neg_log_gmm_DiffFactor_TransformationGeneral.m

-- function to calculate the derivatives of negative log mixture of normals.

obtain_grad_logposterior_logit_skewmix.m

-- function to obtain the gradient of log of the target posterior distribution

SampleFromMixtureDiffFactorTransformationOneAtTimeGeneral.m

-- function to generate sample from the current variational approximation

plot_Logistic.m

-- function to obtain figures in section 4.3

YJ_psi_to_theta.m, YJ_theta_to_psi.m

-- Additional functions used to generate samples from the copula of the mixture.

Other useful functions are provided in the folder.

folder results containing all the results for section 4.3

The user need to add the path to the results folder to generate the figures in section 4.3.